$WW,1$$FG,14$$TX+CX,"TempleNES Game Genie Codes"$$FG$

$TX+CX,"One file per game, named after the ROM"$

TempleNES looks in this folder when a ROM loads.  Load
"Roms/smb1.nes" (or "smb1.nes.Z") and it reads
"Genie/smb1.DD", or "Genie/smb1.DD.Z" if that's what it
finds.  Same name as the ROM, ".DD" instead of ".nes".

$FG,11$G$FG$ then pops up the list with a check box per line.
$FG,11$Space$FG$ checks a line, $FG,11$ON$FG$ turns the checked ones on and
everything else off, and $FG,11$OFF$FG$ turns the lot off without
losing your check marks.  $FG,11$ON + RESET$FG$ also resets the
console, which codes that patch the game's start up
need before they do anything.

$FG,10$Line Format$FG$

  One cheat per line: the code, then $FG,11$two or more spaces$FG$
  (or a tab), then the description.

SXIOPO        Infinite lives for both players

  Cheats that need several codes join them with " + ":

OZTLLX + AATLGZ + SZLIVO        Never shrink, once you've got a mushroom

  Only the description shows in the picker, so say what
  the cheat does, not what the code is.  Keep it under
  70 characters or it gets cut off.

$FG,10$Rules$FG$

  Codes are the 6 or 8 letter kind, from the letters
  A P Z L G I T Y E O X U K S V N.  A line whose codes
  don't decode is skipped and counted in the picker, so
  a typo shows up instead of silently doing nothing.

  Blank lines are fine.  Lines starting with "//" are
  comments.  Anything else that isn't a code counts as
  a bad line, so comment your notes.

  Up to 64 lines per file, and up to 32 codes can run at
  once (a three code cheat spends three of them).

$FG,10$Example$FG$

// Super Mario Bros.
AATOZA        Start players 1 & 2 with 1 life
SXIOPO        Infinite lives for both players
APZLGK        Super jump from a standing start only
YSAOPE + YEAOZA + PEAPYA        Start on World 2

